// hypergraph_chain.vo.expected: expected VO derived by hand from doc/formal (ir_vo.tex WF-VO-*, passes.tex I1-I5
// and the planner O-/S-/R- rules), independently of the producer.
// Every step is preceded by its ordering rule; deterministic tie-breaks are stated below.
// Planner hypergraph = Plan-Graph: O_{Written,Coarse}; acyclic -> R-Tree.
// c0=Edge(a,b), c1=Edge(b,c), c2=Edge(d,c)
// GYO: (0,a) private, (2,d) private, absorb (0,1) pi(0)=1, (1,b) private, absorb (1,2) pi(1)=2, (2,c) private ->
// G-Accept. H-JoinTree = [(0,1),(1,2)], root 2.
// Y-Up/Y-Down with B=BFS(J)=[2,1,0]: up = [red(pi(b),b) | b in reverse([1,0])] = red(1,0), red(2,1); down =
// [red(b,pi(b)) | b in [1,0]] = red(1,2), red(0,1).
// R-Tree: insertAtReadyPrefix = before the first atom. Support columns per WF-VO-Reductions (shared classes
// kept, others _).
struct OrientedChain ; relation Edge (src : i32 [0] , dst : i32 [0]) ; answer (a , d) : - Edge (a , b) , Edge (b , c) , Edge (d , c) ;
valuation {
    // Y-Up 1st: red(pi(0)=1, 0)
    reduce Edge @ 1 with Edge @ 0 (_ , b) ;
    // Y-Up 2nd: red(pi(1)=2, 1)
    reduce Edge @ 2 with Edge @ 1 (_ , c) ;
    // Y-Down 1st: red(1, pi(1)=2)
    reduce Edge @ 1 with Edge @ 2 (_ , c) ;
    // Y-Down 2nd: red(0, pi(0)=1)
    reduce Edge @ 0 with Edge @ 1 (b , _) ;
    // S-Written 0
    Edge @ 0 (a , b) ;
    // S-Written 1
    Edge @ 1 (b , c) ;
    // S-Written 2
    Edge @ 2 (d , c) ;
}
